  "strategy": "1. **Approach and rationale**\n\nThis strategy for improving the Erd\u0151s minimum overlap constant C is based on **progressive resolution optimization** coupled with **structured perturbations**. Unlike traditional random search, it leverages the hierarchical relationship between grids: a function represented at coarser grids (45 points) is interpolated to finer grids (180 points) and optimized locally. This gradient-style approach responds to the non-convex structure of the problem by:\n\n- **Exploring multiple resolutions** sequentially, transferring valid patterns across scales\n- **Maintaining key properties** (integral normalization, box constraints) through informed transformations\n- **Escaping local optimization traps** by projecting candidates through multiple differentiable transformations\n\nBottleneck addressed: Most optimization approaches get stuck in local minima because they cannot explore the larger picture of solution topology. This method overcomes this by using the 45-point solution as a guide to probe higher resolutions.\n\n2. **Mathematical specification**\n\nVariables:\n- H(x): [0,1]-valued function on [0,2]\n- dx = 2/n_points: grid spacing\n- N_constraints = [45, 90, 180]: levels of resolution\n- C5 objective = max\u2096 \u222b\u2089 h(x)(1-h(x+k)) dx: continuous overlap measure\n\nConstrained optimization:\n0 \u2264 h[i] \u2264 1 for all i\n\u222bh dx = 1 exactly\n\nScaled evaluation:\n```python\ndef C5_continous_approx(h):\n    full_corr = np.correlate(h, 1-h, mode='full')\n    max_corr = np.max(full_corr)\n    return dx * max_corr\n```\n\n3. **Implementation procedure**\n\n```python\ndef run(initial_h=None, budget_s=1100):\n    # Time tracking\n    start_time = time.time()\n    best_score = float('inf')\n    best_vector = None\n    \n    # Level init with 45 points\n    if initial_h is None:\n        initial_h = np.random.random(45) * 2 - 1\n    \n    current_vector = initial_h\n    current_n = 45\n    \n    # Projection via water-filling\n    def project_vec(v):\n        total = np.sum(v)\n        target_sum = 45/2  # Current n\n        # Apply water-filling algorithm\n        # Detailed projection implementation as in standard methods\n```",
